  "refinements": [
    "Known native private storage consumes one activated grant before independent root/list publication; scan readiness, semantic completion, result delivery and physical free have separate cuts",
    "Real UTF-8 failure and UDP success paths both decrement still refcount; neither decrement nor caller return class establishes unused credit refund or physical reclamation",
    "PrivateAtomicInit and ScanReadyConstruction have explicit subtype-safe fields/weak/frame metadata, root reload and constructor endpoints; raw allocator wrappers do not qualify independent scanners",
    "Foreign constructor arming preserves one actual native release owner and provider/affinity dependencies; forced still cleanup waits actual constructors and physical users",
    "One heap service owns claim, consume, unused disposal, actual charge and ledger revision; current carried GrantId rather than mint-epoch scalar resolves refund races",
    "Held recount excludes unsafe readers/writers before traversal and settles claimed native effects; actual private/enrolled/detached blocks plus carried/new prepared promises are charged once without double-counting deferred actual words or batch D",
    "Known-live parked deferred release tasks can retain charged storage and roots across GC; do not wait on an owner callback requiring this GC; unknown opaque native free does not qualify as known retained storage",
    "Tail grants use one-section word offsets, target header/body alignment residue, explicit copied-prefix/closure/gap/object-run/overrun/guard layout and exclusive writer rights",
    "Worker retirement preserves VM-owned prefix and actual SectionId; whole-section parser/prepare/sharing/selection/check/statistics paths must be replaced or qualified before interval resume",
    "Pending closure writes and H-to-G completion gaps retain actual transaction/VM custody; timeout/cancel never restores donor rights or recycles live suffix objects",
    "Ten matched support rows, six maintenance events and five net conditions credit modern C helpers, generators and existing native support; tail reuse may be zero and no positive total or Zig-only bound is established"
  ],
